task: sentence_register_detection
instructions: |
  For each item, identify the sentence register as exactly one of:
  informal, standard, formal.

  Use the Hindi and romanisation, not only the English translation.

  Register guide:
  - informal: casual/intimate speech with tum/tu forms, close friends/family,
    teasing, slang, or deliberately casual particles.
  - standard: neutral everyday speech, including polite-but-normal speech with
    āp/āpkā, respectful names, or ordinary classroom/workplace questions.
  - formal: highly respectful, official, ceremonial, deferential, or distant
    speech; strong honorific style or public/official address.

  Important: direct address is not automatically informal. Polite forms such as
  बताइए / batāie, कीजिए / kījie, आइए / āie, आप / āp, आपका / āpkā, and
  honorific/plural agreement usually mean standard or formal, not informal.

  Examples:
    - "प्रकाश, बताइए, आपका मेहमान प्रताप – वह क्या करता है?"
      "Prakāś, batāie, āpkā mehmān Pratāp – vah kyā kartā hai?"
      register: standard
      reason: polite imperative and āpkā; conversational but respectful
    - "कैसे हो प्रताप?"
      "kaise ho Pratāp?"
      register: informal
      reason: ho form implies tum-level familiar address
    - "शर्मा जी गोश्त नहीं खाते।"
      "Śarmā jī gośt nahī̃ khāte."
      register: standard
      reason: respectful ji, but ordinary factual sentence

  Return raw YAML only. Do not wrap the response in markdown fences. Do not add
  prose before or after the YAML.

  Required shape:
  results:
    - id: "0001"
      register: standard
      rationale: "Short reason."
items:
{{#each items}}
  - id: "{{id}}"
    hindi: "{{hindi}}"
    romanisation: "{{romanisation}}"
    english: "{{english}}"
{{/each}}
